=head1 NAME

claude-log-to-scenario - draft a raider scenario from a section of a Claude Code session

=head1 SYNOPSIS

    maint/claude-log-to-scenario SESSION --list
    maint/claude-log-to-scenario [--project DIR] SESSION [--from UUID] [--turns N]
        [--title TEXT] [--root DIR] [--home DIR] [-o FILE]

    maint/claude-log-to-scenario 1eccd093 --list
    maint/claude-log-to-scenario 1eccd093-ac1a-4db8-944c-edc0621ec6f3 --from 787db9a7 --turns 4 \
        -o t/scenarios/claude-logs/50-skill-then-read.yml

=head1 DESCRIPTION

Reads a Claude Code session log (the JSONL file Claude Code keeps under
F<~/.claude/projects/E<lt>projectE<gt>/E<lt>sessionE<gt>.jsonl>) and writes the
chosen section of it as a scenario in the format of F<t/200_scenarios.t> (the
keys are documented in F<t/lib/Test/Raider/Scenario.pm>): what Claude Code's
model answered becomes the C<script:> of raider's scripted model, and what
Claude Code's tools answered becomes the C<expect:> raider's real tools have
to meet. The output is a B<draft> to curate, never a finished test; its head
comment says so.

=over

=item * A step of C<script:> is one model response. Claude Code writes one
response over several lines with the same C<message.id> (a line per content
block); they are put back together. Thinking blocks are left out. A response
with tool calls becomes C<tool_calls:> (its text goes into a comment), one
with text only becomes C<text:>.

=item * Tool names and arguments are translated by
L<Langertha::Raider::ToolNames> (C<Read> becomes C<read_file> with C<path>,
C<Agent> becomes C<agent>, the C<Bash> timeout becomes seconds, ...).
C<MultiEdit> becomes one C<edit_file> per edit. A tool raider does not have
(C<ToolSearch>, C<SendMessage>, C<Monitor>, ...) and every C<mcp__*> tool (a
scenario mounts no MCP server) is left out and noted in a comment.

=item * Paths: under the project root (the C<cwd> the log records, or
C<--root>) they become relative; under the home (C<$HOME>, or C<--home>)
C<{{HOME}}/...>; a file tool call on any other path is left out and noted. In
every other string of a tool call the root becomes C<{{ROOT}}> and the home
C<{{HOME}}>, which the scenario runner fills in; in the prompt and the model's
texts the root is dropped (C<lib/A.pm>, C<.>) and the home becomes C<~>, as
those are compared literally.

=item * C<files:> (and C<home:>) are rebuilt from what the session shows of
each file before it was changed: a C<Read> that returned the whole file, or
the C<originalFile> Claude Code records for an C<Edit> or a C<Write> over an
existing file. A file read only in part, or edited without a recorded
original, is not rebuilt and noted.

=item * C<expect:> lists every tool call with its name and C<error: true>
where Claude Code's call failed, a short regex anchor (the first line of the
file) for a C<read_file> that read a whole file, and the last text as the
C<answer>. Claude Code's error text goes into a comment: raider words its
errors differently. C<bash> gets no anchor: its output depends on the machine.

=item * Secrets are replaced by C<REDACTED> everywhere, comments included:
API keys (C<sk-...>, C<ghp_...>, C<github_pat_...>, C<AKIA...>, C<xox?-...>,
C<AIza...>, C<glpat-...>, C<npm_...>), JWTs, private key blocks, bearer and
basic credentials, passwords in URLs and the value of every assignment whose
name says key, token, secret, password or credential. It errs on the side of
too much.

=item * Subagents. Claude Code writes a subagent's turns into a log of its
own, F<E<lt>sessionE<gt>/subagents/agent-E<lt>agentIdE<gt>.jsonl>, beside an
F<agent-E<lt>agentIdE<gt>.meta.json> naming the C<Agent> call
(C<toolUseId>); the C<agentId> of the call's result names it too. Raider's
scripted model serves a subagent's requests from the same C<script:>, in the
order they are made, and runs the C<agent> calls of one response one after
the other. So after the response with the C<agent> call come the responses of
that subagent's first run (up to the next message to it, a C<SendMessage> of
the caller, which is left out and noted), then those of the next subagent,
then the caller's next response; nested subagents the same way, with
C<app: { max_agent_depth: N }> when they go deeper than raider's default of
1. In C<expect: tools:> a subagent's calls come before those of the response
that started it, as raider records them, and the C<agent> call is anchored on
the subagent's answer. A subagent that hands its report back with
C<SubagentHandback> answers with its message (raider's subagent answers with
its last text); what it did after that is left out. One that ends without
text answers C<done>.

=item * Agent types. A C<subagent_type> that is an agent file in the
project's F<.claude/agents/> (found the way raider finds it) goes into
C<files:> through the same redaction, without its C<skills:> and
C<briefing:> keys: their skills are not in the scenario, and raider refuses
to start an agent whose skills it cannot resolve. Every other type -- Claude
Code's own (C<Explore>, C<Plan>, ...), a user or plugin agent, an agent file
that is gone or unreadable -- becomes C<general-purpose>, raider's one
built-in agent, and is noted.

=item * An C<Agent> call without a subagent log: run in the foreground, the
subagent answers at once with what Claude Code returned (without the
C<agentId>/C<usage> lines it appends); run in the background or failed, the
call is left out and noted. A background agent with a log runs to its end in
raider, at the call: raider has no background subagents.

=back

Sidechain records in the session's own log (C<isSidechain>, not tied to a
call) are skipped; given a subagent's log those are its turns.

=head1 OPTIONS

=over

=item SESSION

The session log: a path, or a session id (also the start of one, or an
C<agent-...> id) looked up in F<$CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR/projects/*/> (default
F<~/.claude/projects>), including the subagent logs.

=item --project DIR

Look the session id up only in this project directory: a path, or a name
under F<projects/> (C<-home-getty-dev-skilletor>).

=item --list

Print the prompts and the model responses of the session, each with its
record id, and exit. An C<Agent> call shows its subagent log and how many
responses its first run has (C<Agent[agent-a1b2.jsonl, 5 responses]>), or
C<Agent[no subagent log]>.

=item --from UUID

The record to start at (a unique prefix will do): a user prompt (the prompt
of the scenario, the section starts after it) or a model response (the section
starts with it; the prompt is the last one before). Default: the first prompt.

=item --turns N

How many model responses of the session to take (the responses of the
subagents they start come along and do not count). A user prompt among them
starts the next of C<prompts:>. Default: up to the next user prompt.

=item --title TEXT

The C<title:>. Default: the first line of the prompt.

=item --root DIR

The project root of the session. Default: the C<cwd> of the first record taken.

=item --home DIR

The home of the session. Default: C<$HOME>.

=item -o FILE, --output FILE

Where to write the scenario. Default: standard output.

=back

=head1 LIMITS

=over

=item * The scenario's C<bash> calls run for real when it is run. A command
naming a path outside the home still names that real path: read every command
before running a draft.

=item * What a C<bash> command did to files is unknown: a file a command
created or changed before the model read it is rebuilt as the model saw it.

=item * A subagent in the background ran beside its caller in Claude Code;
in the draft it runs at the call, so a file it changed may be rebuilt as the
caller saw it later, and the caller's C<agent> result is the subagent's
answer, not Claude Code's launch notice (noted). The task notification that
told Claude Code's model it finished stays a prompt.

=item * A subagent Claude Code started in a worktree of its own runs in the
root: its paths keep the worktree's place below the root
(F<.claude/worktrees/NAME/...>), its relative C<bash> commands do not.

=item * An agent file goes in without its skills; to test the briefing, add
them (F<.claude/skills/E<lt>nameE<gt>/SKILL.md>) and the keys back.

=item * Old logs (before C<toolUseResult>) carry a whole file only as the
numbered result text; its last newline is assumed.

=item * The secret patterns are patterns: a secret in another shape passes.
Read the draft before committing it.

=back

=cut

my $JSON  = JSON::MaybeXS->new( utf8 => 1, canonical => 1, convert_blessed => 1 );
my $YAML  = YAML::PP->new( boolean => 'JSON::PP', preserve => PRESERVE_FLOW_STYLE | PRESERVE_ORDER, width => 1000 );
my $TRUE  = JSON::MaybeXS->true;
my $tools = 'Langertha::Raider::ToolNames';
my $agents = 'Langertha::Raider::Context::Agents';

# Claude Code's own agent types besides general-purpose: raider has none of them.
my %CLAUDE_AGENT = map { $_ => 1 } qw( Explore Plan claude claude-code-guide output-style-setup statusline-setup );

# Keys written first in a flow mapping, the way the hand-written scenarios read.
my %KEY_RANK = (
  name => 0, path => 1, command => 1, pattern => 1,
  error => 2, old_string => 2, content => 2, text => 3, new_string => 3,
);

my @SECRET_RE = (
  qr/-----BEGIN [A-Z0-9 ]*PRIVATE KEY-----.*?-----END [A-Z0-9 ]*PRIVATE KEY-----/s,
  qr/\bsk-[A-Za-z0-9_-]{16,}/,
  qr/\bgh[pousr]_[A-Za-z0-9]{20,}/,
  qr/\bgithub_pat_[A-Za-z0-9_]{20,}/,
  qr/\b(?:AKIA|ASIA)[0-9A-Z]{16}\b/,
  qr/\bxox[abposr]-[A-Za-z0-9-]{10,}/,
  qr/\bAIza[0-9A-Za-z_-]{35}/,
  qr/\bglpat-[A-Za-z0-9_-]{20,}/,
  qr/\bnpm_[A-Za-z0-9]{36}/,
  qr/\b[0-9]{8,10}:AA[A-Za-z0-9_-]{30,}/,
  qr/\beyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]{8,}\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]{8,}\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]+/,
);
my $SECRET_NAME = qr/[A-Za-z0-9_.-]*(?:key|token|secret|passw(?:or)?d|passphrase|credential|private)[A-Za-z0-9_]*/i;

sub main {
  my %opt;
  GetOptions(
    'project=s'  => \$opt{project},
    'list'       => \$opt{list},
    'from=s'     => \$opt{from},
    'turns=i'    => \$opt{turns},
    'title=s'    => \$opt{title},
    'root=s'     => \$opt{root},
    'home=s'     => \$opt{home},
    'output|o=s' => \$opt{output},
    'help|h'     => \$opt{help},
  ) or pod2usage(2);
  pod2usage( -verbose => 2, -exitval => 0 ) if $opt{help};
  pod2usage(2) unless @ARGV == 1;
  pod2usage( -message => '--turns must be at least 1', -exitval => 2 ) if defined $opt{turns} && $opt{turns} < 1;

  my $log = read_log( find_session( $ARGV[0], $opt{project} ) );
  if ( $opt{list} ) {
    list_events($log);
    return 0;
  }
  my $yaml = scenario_yaml( $log, select_section( $log, \%opt ), \%opt );
  if ( defined $opt{output} ) {
    path( $opt{output} )->touchpath->spew_utf8($yaml);
  }
  else {
    print $yaml;
  }
  return 0;
}

#### The session log

sub find_session {
  my ( $arg, $project ) = @_;
  my $file = path($arg);
  return $file if $file->is_file;
  croak 'No session log '.$arg if $arg =~ m{/};
  my $config   = defined $ENV{CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR} ? path( $ENV{CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR} ) : path( $ENV{HOME} // '.', '.claude' );
  my $projects = $config->child('projects');
  my @dirs = defined $project
    ? ( path($project)->is_dir ? path($project) : $projects->child($project) )
    : ( $projects->is_dir ? grep { $_->is_dir } $projects->children : () );
  ( my $id = $arg ) =~ s/\.jsonl\z//;
  my @hits;
  for my $dir ( grep { $_->is_dir } @dirs ) {
    push @hits, grep { $_->basename =~ /\A\Q$id\E/ } $dir->children(qr/\.jsonl\z/);
    for my $sub ( grep { $_->child('subagents')->is_dir } $dir->children ) {
      push @hits, grep { $_->basename =~ /\A\Q$id\E/ } $sub->child('subagents')->children(qr/\.jsonl\z/);
    }
  }
  croak 'No session '.$id.' under '.( defined $project ? $project : $projects ) unless @hits;
  croak 'Session '.$id.' is not unique: '.join( ', ', sort map {"$_"} @hits ) if @hits > 1;
  return $hits[0];
}

# The conversation of the log as events in order: prompts (a user's text) and
# steps (one model response, its blocks gathered over every line of its
# message id), plus the tool results by tool_use id.
sub read_log {
  my ( $file ) = @_;
  my @records;
  for my $line ( $file->lines_raw ) {
    my $r = eval { $JSON->decode($line) };
    push @records, $r if ref $r eq 'HASH' && ( $r->{type} // '' ) =~ /\A(?:user|assistant)\z/;
  }
  croak 'No conversation in '.$file unless @records;
  my $side = !grep { !$_->{isSidechain} } @records;   # a subagent's own log
  @records = grep { !!$_->{isSidechain} == $side } @records;

  my ( @events, %step_of, %event_of, %result_of );
  for my $r (@records) {
    my $content = ref $r->{message} eq 'HASH' ? $r->{message}{content} : undef;
    if ( $r->{type} eq 'assistant' ) {
      my $id   = $r->{message}{id} // $r->{uuid};
      my $step = $step_of{$id} //= do {
        my $s = { kind => 'step', id => $id, uuid => $r->{uuid}, time => $r->{timestamp}, cwd => $r->{cwd}, blocks => [] };
        push @events, $s;
        $s;
      };
      push @{ $step->{blocks} }, ref $content eq 'ARRAY' ? @$content : defined $content ? { type => 'text', text => $content } : ();
      $event_of{ $r->{uuid} } = $step if defined $r->{uuid};
      next;
    }
    my @results = ref $content eq 'ARRAY' ? grep { ( $_->{type} // '' ) eq 'tool_result' } @$content : ();
    if (@results) {
      for my $b (@results) {
        $result_of{ $b->{tool_use_id} } = { block => $b, @results == 1 ? ( data => $r->{toolUseResult} ) : () };
      }
      $event_of{ $r->{uuid} } = { kind => 'result' } if defined $r->{uuid};
      next;
    }
    my $text = prompt_text($r) // next;
    my $e = { kind => 'prompt', uuid => $r->{uuid}, time => $r->{timestamp}, cwd => $r->{cwd}, text => $text };
    push @events, $e;
    $event_of{ $r->{uuid} } = $e if defined $r->{uuid};
  }
  return { file => $file, events => \@events, event_of => \%event_of, result_of => \%result_of };
}

# Claude Code keeps a subagent's turns in a log of its own,
# <session>/subagents/agent-<agentId>.jsonl, beside agent-<agentId>.meta.json
# that names the Agent call (toolUseId). A subagent's log has its nested
# subagents in the same directory.
sub subagent_dir {
  my ( $log ) = @_;
  my $file = $log->{file};
  return $file->parent if $file->parent->basename eq 'subagents';
  return $file->parent->child( $file->basename('.jsonl'), 'subagents' );
}

sub subagent_logs {
  my ( $log ) = @_;
  return $log->{subagents} //= do {
    my $dir = subagent_dir($log);
    my %by_call;
    for my $meta ( $dir->is_dir ? $dir->children(qr/\.meta\.json\z/) : () ) {
      my $m = eval { $JSON->decode( $meta->slurp_raw ) };
      next unless ref $m eq 'HASH' && defined $m->{toolUseId};
      ( my $name = $meta->basename ) =~ s/\.meta\.json\z/.jsonl/;
      $by_call{ $m->{toolUseId} } = $dir->child($name) if $dir->child($name)->is_file;
    }
    \%by_call;
  };
}

# The log of the subagent an Agent call started: by its meta file, else by
# the agentId of the call's result.
sub subagent_log_file {
  my ( $log, $use, $result ) = @_;
  my $file = subagent_logs($log)->{ $use->{id} // '' };
  return $file if $file;
  my $data = $result ? $result->{data} : undef;
  my $id   = ref $data eq 'HASH' ? $data->{agentId} : undef;
  return unless defined $id && $id =~ /\A[\w-]+\z/;
  $file = subagent_dir($log)->child( 'agent-'.$id.'.jsonl' );
  return $file->is_file ? $file : undef;
}

# The model responses of a subagent's first run: those after its prompt, up
# to the next message to it (a SendMessage of the caller), and whether more
# came after.
sub subagent_steps {
  my ( $sub ) = @_;
  my @events = @{ $sub->{events} };
  shift @events while @events && $events[0]{kind} ne 'prompt';
  shift @events;
  my @steps;
  while ( @events && $events[0]{kind} eq 'step' ) { push @steps, shift @events }
  return ( \@steps, scalar grep { $_->{kind} eq 'step' } @events );
}

sub is_agent_call {
  my ( $use ) = @_;
  return ( $use->{type} // '' ) eq 'tool_use' && ( $tools->raider_name( $use->{name} // '?' ) // '' ) eq 'agent';
}

sub is_background {
  my ( $use, $result ) = @_;
  my $data = $result ? $result->{data} : undef;
  my $flag = ref $use->{input} eq 'HASH' ? $use->{input}{run_in_background} : undef;
  return 1 if $flag && "$flag" !~ /\A(?:false|0)\z/i;
  return ref $data eq 'HASH' && ( $data->{isAsync} || ( $data->{status} // '' ) eq 'async_launched' ) ? 1 : 0;
}

sub prompt_text {
  my ( $r ) = @_;
  return if $r->{isMeta} || $r->{isCompactSummary} || $r->{isVisibleInTranscriptOnly};
  my $c    = $r->{message}{content};
  my $text = ref $c eq 'ARRAY'
    ? join( "\n\n", map { $_->{text} // '' } grep { ( $_->{type} // '' ) eq 'text' } @$c )
    : $c;
  return unless defined $text;
  $text = strip_reminders($text);
  return if $text =~ /\A\s*\z/
    || $text =~ /\A\[Request interrupted/
    || $text =~ /\A\s*<(?:command-name|command-message|command-args|local-command-\w+|bash-\w+)>/;
  return $text;
}

sub strip_reminders {
  my ( $text ) = @_;
  $text =~ s{\s*<system-reminder>.*?</system-reminder>\s*}{\n}gs;
  $text =~ s/\A\n+//;
  $text =~ s/\n+\z/\n/ if $text =~ /\n\z/;
  return $text;
}

sub list_events {
  my ( $log ) = @_;
  for my $e ( @{ $log->{events} } ) {
    my $what = $e->{kind} eq 'prompt'
      ? 'PROMPT  '.one_line( $e->{text}, 90 )
      : 'MODEL   '.join( ' ', map {
          is_agent_call($_) ? $_->{name}.'['.list_subagent( $log, $_ ).']'
          : $_->{type} eq 'tool_use' ? $_->{name} : $_->{type} eq 'text' ? '"'.one_line( $_->{text}, 40 ).'"' : ()
        } @{ $e->{blocks} } );
    print join( '  ', $e->{uuid} // '-', $e->{time} // '-', redact($what) ), "\n";
  }
}

sub list_subagent {
  my ( $log, $use ) = @_;
  my $file = subagent_log_file( $log, $use, $log->{result_of}{ $use->{id} // '' } ) or return 'no subagent log';
  my $sub  = eval { read_log($file) } or return $file->basename.', unreadable';
  my ( $steps ) = subagent_steps($sub);
  return $file->basename.', '.@$steps.' response'.( @$steps == 1 ? '' : 's' );
}

sub one_line {
  my ( $text, $max ) = @_;
  my ( $line ) = grep { /\S/ } split /\n/, $text // '';
  $line //= '';
  $line =~ s/\A\s+|\s+\z//g;
  return length $line > $max ? substr( $line, 0, $max - 3 ).'...' : $line;
}

#### The section

sub select_section {
  my ( $log, $opt ) = @_;
  my @events = @{ $log->{events} };
  my $start;
  if ( defined $opt->{from} ) {
    my $from = $opt->{from};
    my @hits = grep { index( $_, $from ) == 0 } keys %{ $log->{event_of} };
    croak 'No record '.$from.' in '.$log->{file} unless @hits;
    croak 'Record '.$from.' is not unique: '.join( ', ', sort @hits ) if @hits > 1;
    $start = $log->{event_of}{ $hits[0] };
    croak 'Record '.$hits[0].' is a tool result: start at a prompt or a model response' if $start->{kind} eq 'result';
  }
  else {
    ($start) = grep { $_->{kind} eq 'prompt' } @events;
    croak 'No prompt in '.$log->{file}.': pick a model response with --from' unless $start;
  }
  my ($i) = grep { $events[$_] == $start } 0 .. $#events;

  my @spans;
  if ( $start->{kind} eq 'prompt' ) {
    push @spans, { prompt => $start->{text}, steps => [] };
    $i++;
  }
  else {
    my ($before) = grep { $_->{kind} eq 'prompt' } reverse @events[ 0 .. $i - 1 ];
    push @spans, { prompt => $before ? $before->{text} : undef, steps => [] };
  }
  my $taken = 0;
  for my $e ( @events[ $i .. $#events ] ) {
    if ( $e->{kind} eq 'prompt' ) {
      last unless defined $opt->{turns};
      push @spans, { prompt => $e->{text}, steps => [] };
      next;
    }
    push @{ $spans[-1]{steps} }, $e;
    last if defined $opt->{turns} && ++$taken >= $opt->{turns};
  }
  pop @spans while @spans > 1 && !@{ $spans[-1]{steps} };
  croak 'The section has no model response' unless grep { @{ $_->{steps} } } @spans;
  return { start => $start, spans => \@spans, taken => scalar map { @{ $_->{steps} } } @spans };
}

#### Paths, placeholders, secrets

sub context_for {
  my ( $log, $section, $opt ) = @_;
  my $root = $opt->{root} // $section->{start}{cwd}
    // croak 'The log records no cwd: give the project root with --root';
  my $home = $opt->{home} // $ENV{HOME} // croak 'No home: give it with --home';
  s{/+\z}{} for $root, $home;
  return {
    root => $root, home => $home,
    files => {}, home_files => {}, decided => {}, file_notes => [],
    depth => 0, sub_steps => 0, agent_types => {},
  };
}

# A path as the scenario names it: relative under the root, {{HOME}}/... under
# the home; undef elsewhere.
sub map_path {
  my ( $ctx, $p ) = @_;
  return $p unless $p =~ m{\A/};
  my ( $where, $rel ) = place( $ctx, $p );
  return unless $where;
  return $where eq 'files' ? $rel : $rel eq '.' ? '{{HOME}}' : '{{HOME}}/'.$rel;
}

sub place {
  my ( $ctx, $p ) = @_;
  $p =~ s{/+\z}{} unless $p eq '/';
  for ( [ files => $ctx->{root} ], [ home => $ctx->{home} ] ) {
    my ( $where, $base ) = @$_;
    return ( $where, '.' ) if $p eq $base;
    return ( $where, substr( $p, length($base) + 1 ) ) if index( $p, $base.'/' ) == 0;
  }
  return;
}

# Inside tool arguments and file contents: the runner fills the placeholders.
sub fill_placeholders {
  my ( $ctx, $text ) = @_;
  my ( $root, $home ) = @{$ctx}{qw( root home )};
  $text =~ s{\Q$root\E(?![\w.-])}{\{\{ROOT\}\}}g;
  $text =~ s{\Q$home\E(?![\w.-])}{\{\{HOME\}\}}g;
  return $text;
}

# In texts compared literally (prompt, answers, comments).
sub plain_paths {
  my ( $ctx, $text ) = @_;
  my ( $root, $home ) = @{$ctx}{qw( root home )};
  $text =~ s{\Q$root\E/}{}g;
  $text =~ s{\Q$root\E(?![\w.-])}{.}g;
  $text =~ s{\Q$home\E(?![\w.-])}{~}g;
  return $text;
}

sub deep {
  my ( $code, $v ) = @_;
  return ref $v eq 'HASH' ? { map { $_ => deep( $code, $v->{$_} ) } keys %$v }
       : ref $v eq 'ARRAY' ? [ map { deep( $code, $_ ) } @$v ]
       : defined $v && !ref $v ? $code->($v)
       : $v;
}


sub redact {
  my ( $text ) = @_;
  return $text unless defined $text;
  $text =~ s/$_/REDACTED/g for @SECRET_RE;
  $text =~ s{\b(Bearer|Basic)(\s+)[A-Za-z0-9._~+/=-]{8,}}{$1$2REDACTED}g;
  $text =~ s{(Authorization:\s*token\s+)\S+}{$1REDACTED}gi;
  $text =~ s{(\b[a-z][a-z0-9+.-]*://[^/\s:@'"]+:)[^/\s@'"]+@}{$1REDACTED@}gi;
  $text =~ s/([\$\@%]?)\b($SECRET_NAME)(["']?\s*(?:=>|(?<![:=!<>])=(?!=)|(?<!:):(?!:))\s*)(["']?)([^\s"',;)]+)/redact_assignment( $1, $2, $3, $4, $5 )/ge;
  return $text;
}

# NAME=value, NAME: value, NAME => 'value': the value goes, unless it is
# plainly no secret -- code ($token = shift, os.environ["X"]), a short or
# punctuation-only word, a small number, a keyword.
sub redact_assignment {
  my ( $sigil, $name, $op, $quote, $value ) = @_;
  my $bare = !$quote;
  my $kept = ( $bare && ( $sigil || $value =~ m{\A[\$\@%&(\[\{<>=!~\\/-]} || $value =~ m{[(\[]} ) )
    || ( $bare && ( length $value < 4 || $value !~ /[A-Za-z0-9]/ ) )
    || $value =~ /\A(?:[0-9]{1,6}|true|false|null|undef|none|yes|no|REDACTED.*)\z/i;
  return $sigil.$name.$op.$quote.( $kept ? $value : 'REDACTED' );
}

#### Tool calls

sub result_text {
  my ( $result ) = @_;
  return '' unless $result;
  my $c = $result->{block}{content};
  return ref $c eq 'ARRAY' ? join( "\n", map { $_->{text} // '' } grep { ( $_->{type} // '' ) eq 'text' } @$c ) : $c // '';
}

# The whole content of a file a Read returned, or (undef, why not).
sub read_content {
  my ( $use, $result ) = @_;
  return ( undef, 'no result in the log' ) unless $result;
  return ( undef, 'the read failed' ) if $result->{block}{is_error};
  my $data = $result->{data};
  if ( ref $data eq 'HASH' && exists $data->{file} ) {
    return ( undef, 'not a text file ('.( $data->{type} // '?' ).')' )
      unless ( $data->{type} // '' ) eq 'text' && ref $data->{file} eq 'HASH';
    my $f = $data->{file};
    return $f->{content}
      if ( $f->{startLine} // 1 ) == 1 && defined $f->{numLines} && defined $f->{totalLines}
        && $f->{numLines} == $f->{totalLines} && defined $f->{content};
    return ( undef, 'read only in part (lines '.( $f->{startLine} // '?' ).' to '
      .( ( $f->{startLine} // 1 ) + ( $f->{numLines} // 0 ) - 1 ).' of '.( $f->{totalLines} // '?' ).')' );
  }
  return ( undef, 'not a text file' ) if ref $data eq 'HASH';
  my $in = $use->{input} // {};
  return ( undef, 'read only in part' ) if defined $in->{offset} || defined $in->{limit};
  my @lines = split /\n/, strip_reminders( result_text($result) ), -1;
  pop @lines if @lines && $lines[-1] eq '';
  return ( undef, 'the result is empty' ) unless @lines;
  my ( $n, @out ) = (0);
  for my $line (@lines) {
    return ( undef, 'the result is not numbered line by line' )
      unless $line =~ /\A\s*([0-9]+)(?:\t|\x{2192})(.*)\z/s && $1 == ++$n;
    push @out, $2;
  }
  return ( undef, 'possibly cut off at 2000 lines' ) if $n >= 2000;
  return join( "\n", @out )."\n";
}

# What the session shows of a file before the section changed it.
sub learn_file {
  my ( $ctx, $use, $result ) = @_;
  my $name = $use->{name};
  return unless $name =~ /\A(?:Read|Edit|MultiEdit|Write)\z/;
  my $fp = ( $use->{input} // {} )->{file_path};
  return unless defined $fp && $fp =~ m{\A/};
  my ( $where, $rel ) = place( $ctx, $fp );
  return unless $where;
  my $key = $where.'/'.$rel;
  return if $ctx->{decided}{$key};
  my $shown = $where eq 'files' ? $rel : '~/'.$rel;
  my $data  = $result ? $result->{data} : undef;
  my $set   = sub {
    my ( $content ) = @_;
    $ctx->{ $where eq 'files' ? 'files' : 'home_files' }{$rel} = fill_placeholders( $ctx, redact($content) );
    $ctx->{decided}{$key} = 1;
  };
  my $unknown = sub {
    my ( $why, $final ) = @_;
    # one note for the reads in part, one for what settles it
    push @{ $ctx->{file_notes} }, $shown.': '.$why if $final || !$ctx->{noted}{$key}++;
    $ctx->{decided}{$key} = 1 if $final;
  };
  if ( $name eq 'Read' ) {
    if ( $result && $result->{block}{is_error} ) {
      my $why = one_line( result_text($result), 80 );
      return $unknown->( 'its first read failed ('.$why.'), not written', 1 );
    }
    my ( $content, $why ) = read_content( $use, $result );
    return $set->($content) if defined $content;
    return $unknown->( 'not rebuilt, '.$why );
  }
  if ( $name eq 'Write' && ref $data eq 'HASH' && ( $data->{type} // '' ) eq 'create' ) {
    return $ctx->{decided}{$key} = 1;   # did not exist
  }
  return $set->( $data->{originalFile} ) if ref $data eq 'HASH' && defined $data->{originalFile};
  return $unknown->( 'changed by '.$name.' before any whole read, its content is not in the log', 1 );
}

# A Claude Code tool call as raider calls: ( [ [ tool, \%args ], ... ] ) or ( [], note ).
sub translate_call {
  my ( $ctx, $use ) = @_;
  my $name  = $use->{name} // '?';
  my $input = ref $use->{input} eq 'HASH' ? $use->{input} : {};
  return ( [], 'left out '.$name.': an MCP tool, the scenario mounts no MCP server' ) if $tools->is_mcp($name);
  my $tool = $tools->raider_name($name);
  return ( [], 'left out '.$name.': raider has no such tool' ) unless defined $tool;
  my @inputs = $name eq 'MultiEdit'
    ? map { +{ file_path => $input->{file_path}, %$_ } } grep { ref $_ eq 'HASH' } @{ $input->{edits} // [] }
    : ($input);
  my @calls;
  for my $in (@inputs) {
    my $args = $tools->raider_input( $tool, $in );
    my %mapped;
    for my $key ( path_keys( $tool, $args ) ) {
      my $p = map_path( $ctx, $args->{$key} );
      return ( [], 'left out '.$name.' '.$args->{$key}.': outside the project and the home' ) unless defined $p;
      $mapped{$key} = $p;
    }
    $args = deep( sub { fill_placeholders( $ctx, redact( $_[0] ) ) }, $args );
    $args->{$_} = $mapped{$_} for keys %mapped;
    push @calls, [ $tool, $args ];
  }
  return ( \@calls );
}

sub path_keys {
  my ( $tool, $args ) = @_;
  my @keys = $tool =~ /\A(?:read_file|write_file|edit_file|list_files|glob|grep)\z/ ? ('path') : ();
  push @keys, 'pattern' if $tool eq 'glob';
  return grep { defined $args->{$_} && !ref $args->{$_} && $args->{$_} =~ m{\A/} } @keys;
}

sub expectation {
  my ( $ctx, $tool, $use, $result, $run ) = @_;
  my %want = ( name => $tool );
  my @notes;
  if ($run) {
    # raider's agent result is the subagent's last text, which the script gives.
    my ($first) = $run->{answer} =~ /\A\s*([^\n]*)/;
    $first =~ s/\s+\z//;
    $want{text} = '\A\s*'.regex_quote( substr( $first, 0, 40 ) );
    push @notes, "Claude Code's result was only the launch notice: it ran the agent in the background" if $run->{background};
    return ( \%want, \@notes );
  }
  unless ($result) {
    push @notes, 'no result in the log';
    return ( \%want, \@notes );
  }
  if ( $result->{block}{is_error} ) {
    $want{error} = $TRUE;
    push @notes, 'Claude Code: '.one_line( plain_paths( $ctx, redact( result_text($result) ) ), 100 );
    return ( \%want, \@notes );
  }
  if ( $tool eq 'read_file' ) {
    my ($content) = read_content( $use, $result );
    my ($first) = grep { /\S/ } split /\n/, $content // '';
    if ( defined $first ) {
      $first =~ s/\A\s+|\s+\z//g;
      $first = substr( $first, 0, 40 );
      $first = redact($first);
      $want{text} = regex_quote($first)
        unless index( $first, $ctx->{root} ) >= 0 || index( $first, $ctx->{home} ) >= 0;
    }
  }
  return ( \%want, \@notes );
}

sub regex_quote {
  my ( $text ) = @_;
  $text =~ s{([\\.^\$|?*+()\[\]{}])}{\\$1}g;
  return $text;
}

#### Runs and subagents

# What one run puts into the scenario: script items ({ step, comments }),
# tool expectations ({ want, comments }), comments waiting for the next item,
# the last text answer.
sub new_acc { return { items => [], tools => [], pending => [], answer => undef } }

sub push_item {
  my ( $acc, $step, @comments ) = @_;
  push @{ $acc->{items} }, { comments => [ splice( @{ $acc->{pending} } ), @comments ], step => $step };
  $acc->{answer} = $step->{text} if exists $step->{text};
  return;
}

# The model responses of one run (a span of the session, or a subagent's turn)
# in the order raider's scripted model serves them: a response, then the whole
# run of each subagent it starts, in call order, then the next response. A
# subagent's tool results are recorded before those of the response that
# started it, so its expectations come first. True when the run ends on a
# text answer.
sub emit_run {
  my ( $ctx, $log, $steps, $acc, $depth ) = @_;
  my $last_kind = '';
  for my $n ( 0 .. $#$steps ) {
    my $step   = $steps->[$n];
    my @blocks = @{ $step->{blocks} };
    my @texts  = map { $_->{text} } grep { ( $_->{type} // '' ) eq 'text' && defined $_->{text} && $_->{text} =~ /\S/ } @blocks;
    my @uses   = grep { ( $_->{type} // '' ) eq 'tool_use' } @blocks;
    my ($handback) = grep { ( $_->{name} // '' ) eq 'SubagentHandback' } @uses;
    @uses = grep { ( $_->{name} // '' ) ne 'SubagentHandback' } @uses;
    my $text = redact( plain_paths( $ctx, join "\n\n", @texts ) );
    push @{ $acc->{pending} }, 'left out a '.$_->{type}.' block'
      for grep { ( $_->{type} // '' ) =~ /\A(?:server_tool_use|.+_tool_result)\z/ } @blocks;
    if ( !@uses && !$handback ) {
      next unless @texts;
      push_item( $acc, { text => $text } );
      $last_kind = 'text';
      next;
    }
    my ( @calls, @own, @runs );
    my @comments = ( @texts ? 'model: '.one_line( $text, 100 ) : () );
    for my $use (@uses) {
      my $result = $log->{result_of}{ $use->{id} // '' };
      learn_file( $ctx, $use, $result );
      my ( $translated, $note ) = translate_call( $ctx, $use );
      push @comments, plain_paths( $ctx, redact($note) ) if defined $note;
      for my $call (@$translated) {
        my $run;
        if ( $call->[0] eq 'agent' ) {
          ( $run, my @notes ) = subagent_run( $ctx, $log, $use, $result, $call, $depth + 1 );
          push @comments, map { plain_paths( $ctx, redact($_) ) } @notes;
          next unless $run;
          push @runs, $run;
        }
        push @calls, $call;
        my ( $want, $notes ) = expectation( $ctx, $call->[0], $use, $result, $run );
        push @$notes, 'from MultiEdit: Claude Code applies its edits all or none' if $use->{name} eq 'MultiEdit';
        push @own, { want => $want, comments => $notes };
      }
    }
    if (@calls) {
      push_item( $acc, { tool_calls => \@calls }, @comments );
      $last_kind = 'calls';
      for my $run (@runs) {
        my ( $first, @rest ) = @{ $run->{items} };
        push @{ $acc->{items} }, { %$first, comments => [ @{ $acc->{pending} }, @{ $first->{comments} } ] }, @rest;
        @{ $acc->{pending} } = @{ $run->{pending} };
        push @{ $acc->{tools} }, @{ $run->{tools} };
      }
      push @{ $acc->{pending} }, 'back in the caller' if @runs;
      push @{ $acc->{tools} }, @own;
    }
    else {
      push @{ $acc->{pending} }, @comments;
    }
    next unless $handback;
    # Claude Code's subagents hand their report back with a tool; raider's
    # subagent answers with its last text, which ends its run.
    my $message = ref $handback->{input} eq 'HASH' ? $handback->{input}{message} : undef;
    $message = redact( plain_paths( $ctx, defined $message && !ref $message && $message =~ /\S/ ? $message : 'done' ) );
    my $left = $#$steps - $n;
    push_item( $acc, { text => $message }, 'SubagentHandback: its message is the answer' );
    push @{ $acc->{pending} }, 'left out '.$left.' later response'.( $left == 1 ? '' : 's' ).' of this run, after SubagentHandback' if $left;
    return 1;
  }
  return $last_kind eq 'text';
}

# The run of the subagent an agent call starts, replayed from its own log:
# ( { items, tools, pending, answer, background }, notes ), or ( undef, notes )
# when the call is left out. The call's subagent_type may become
# general-purpose (agent_type).
sub subagent_run {
  my ( $ctx, $log, $use, $result, $call, $depth ) = @_;
  my $label = 'Agent ('.one_line( $use->{input}{description} // '', 50 ).')';
  my $background = is_background( $use, $result );
  my $file = subagent_log_file( $log, $use, $result );
  my ( $sub, $steps, $later, $answer );
  if ($file) {
    $sub = eval { read_log($file) };
    return ( undef, 'left out '.$label.': its subagent log '.$file->basename.' has no conversation' ) unless $sub;
    ( $steps, $later ) = subagent_steps($sub);
  }
  elsif ( $background ) {
    return ( undef, 'left out '.$label.': Claude Code ran it in the background and its subagent log is missing' );
  }
  elsif ( !$result || $result->{block}{is_error} ) {
    return ( undef, 'left out '.$label.': '.( $result
      ? 'it failed in Claude Code ('.one_line( result_text($result), 80 ).') and started no subagent'
      : 'no result and no subagent log' ) );
  }
  else {
    $answer = agent_answer($result)
      // return ( undef, 'left out '.$label.': no subagent log and no answer in its result' );
  }
  $ctx->{depth} = $depth if $depth > $ctx->{depth};
  my $type  = $call->[1]{subagent_type} // 'general-purpose';
  my @notes = agent_type( $ctx, $call->[1] );
  $type .= ' (as general-purpose)' if $type ne ( $call->[1]{subagent_type} // 'general-purpose' );

  my $acc = new_acc();
  if ($sub) {
    my $source = 'subagent '.$type.' of '.$label.', from '.$file->basename;
    push @{ $acc->{pending} }, $source.( $background ? ' (Claude Code ran it in the background, raider runs it to the end)' : '' );
    $ctx->{sub_steps} += @$steps;
    push_item( $acc, { text => 'done' }, 'the subagent ends here without a text answer in its log' )
      unless emit_run( $ctx, $sub, $steps, $acc, $depth );
    push @{ $acc->{pending} }, 'its log goes on after a later message to it (SendMessage): '.$later.' more response'.( $later == 1 ? '' : 's' ).' not replayed'
      if $later;
  }
  else {
    push_item( $acc, { text => redact( plain_paths( $ctx, $answer ) ) },
      'subagent of '.$label.': no log of its turns, it answers with what Claude Code returned' );
  }
  return ( { %$acc, background => $background }, @notes );
}

# The subagent's text in an Agent result, without what Claude Code appends.
sub agent_answer {
  my ( $result ) = @_;
  my $text = strip_reminders( result_text($result) );
  $text =~ s/\n*agentId: .*\z//s;
  $text =~ s/\n*<usage>.*\z//s;
  $text =~ s/\A\s+|\s+\z//g;
  return if $text eq '' || $text =~ /\AAsync agent launched|\(its SubagentHandback call\)/;
  return $text;
}

# The agent a call names, as the scenario can give it: an agent file in the
# project's .claude/agents goes into files: (redacted, without the skills it
# declares -- they are not in the scenario and raider refuses a spawn whose
# skills it cannot resolve); any other type becomes general-purpose, raider's
# one built-in agent. Notes for the head of the scenario.
sub agent_type {
  my ( $ctx, $args ) = @_;
  my $type = $args->{subagent_type};
  return if !defined $type || ref $type || $type eq '' || $type eq 'general-purpose';
  my $seen = exists $ctx->{agent_types}{$type};
  my $how  = $ctx->{agent_types}{$type} //= carry_agent( $ctx, $type );
  $args->{subagent_type} = 'general-purpose' unless $how->{keep};
  push @{ $ctx->{file_notes} }, @{ $how->{file_notes} } unless $seen;
  return $how->{keep} ? () : ( 'subagent_type '.$type.': '.$how->{why}.', general-purpose stands in' );
}

sub carry_agent {
  my ( $ctx, $type ) = @_;
  my $standin = sub { return { keep => 0, why => $_[0], file_notes => [] } };
  my $dir   = path( $ctx->{root}, '.claude', 'agents' );
  my $agent = $agents->new( roots => [ { dir => "$dir", source => '.claude/agents' } ] )->find($type);
  return $standin->( $CLAUDE_AGENT{$type}
    ? "Claude Code's built-in agent, raider has no such agent"
    : 'no such agent file in .claude/agents of the project (a user or plugin agent, or gone)' )
    unless $agent && $agent->{file};
  my $file = path( $agent->{file} );
  my $rel  = $file->relative( $ctx->{root} )->stringify;
  my $text = eval { $file->slurp_utf8 } // return $standin->( $rel.' is not readable' );
  my @dropped = @{ $agent->{skills} };
  if (@dropped) {
    $text = drop_skill_keys($text) // return $standin->( $rel.': its skills cannot be taken out of the frontmatter' );
  }
  $text = fill_placeholders( $ctx, redact($text) );
  # what raider reads from the text as it goes into the scenario
  my $check = Path::Tiny->tempdir;
  $check->child( 'agents', $file->basename )->touchpath->spew_utf8($text);
  my $back = $agents->new( roots => [ { dir => $check->child('agents')->stringify, source => 'check' } ] )->find($type);
  return $standin->( $rel.' does not read back as the same agent once redacted' )
    unless $back && $back->{file} && !@{ $back->{skills} } && $back->{description} eq $agent->{description};
  $ctx->{files}{$rel} = $text;
  $ctx->{decided}{ 'files/'.$rel } = 1;
  return { keep => 1, file_notes => [
    $rel.': the agent '.$type.', from the project'.( @dropped ? ', without its skills ('.join( ', ', @dropped ).')' : '' ),
  ] };
}

# An agent file without its top-level skills: and briefing: keys.
sub drop_skill_keys {
  my ( $text ) = @_;
  my ( $open, $fm, $rest ) = $text =~ /\A(---[ \t]*\r?\n)(.*?\r?\n)?(---[ \t]*(?:\r?\n.*)?)\z/s or return;
  my ( @out, $dropping );
  for my $line ( split /(?<=\n)/, $fm // '' ) {
    if ( $line =~ /\A(?:skills|briefing)[ \t]*:/ ) { $dropping = 1; next }
    next if $dropping && $line =~ /\A(?:[ \t]|-(?:[ \t]|\r?\n)|\r?\n)/;
    $dropping = 0;
    push @out, $line;
  }
  return $open.join( '', @out ).$rest;
}

#### The scenario

sub scenario_yaml {
  my ( $log, $section, $opt ) = @_;
  my $ctx = context_for( $log, $section, $opt );

  my @prompts;
  my $acc = new_acc();
  for my $span ( @{ $section->{spans} } ) {
    push @prompts, defined $span->{prompt} ? redact( plain_paths( $ctx, $span->{prompt} ) ) : undef;
    next if emit_run( $ctx, $log, $span->{steps}, $acc, 0 );
    # raider ends a run on a text answer; a turn that stopped elsewhere gets one.
    push_item( $acc, { text => 'done' }, 'the turn ends here without a text answer in the log' );
  }
  my @items   = @{ $acc->{items} };
  my @tools   = @{ $acc->{tools} };
  my @pending = @{ $acc->{pending} };
  my $answer  = $acc->{answer};

  my %doc;
  $doc{title} = $opt->{title} // default_title( $ctx, $log, \@prompts );
  my $no_prompt = !defined $prompts[0];
  $prompts[0] //= 'go';
  if ( @prompts > 1 ) { $doc{prompts} = \@prompts } else { $doc{prompt} = $prompts[0] }
  $doc{app}    = { max_agent_depth => $ctx->{depth} } if $ctx->{depth} > 1;
  $doc{files}  = $ctx->{files}      if %{ $ctx->{files} };
  $doc{home}   = $ctx->{home_files} if %{ $ctx->{home_files} };
  $doc{script} = [ map { $_->{step} } @items ];
  $doc{expect} = { answer => $answer, @tools ? ( tools => [ map { $_->{want} } @tools ] ) : () };

  my $out = header( $log, $section, $ctx );
  $out .= dump_key( 0, title => $doc{title} );
  $out .= "# no user prompt before the section: a placeholder\n" if $no_prompt;
  $out .= exists $doc{prompts} ? dump_key( 0, prompts => $doc{prompts} ) : dump_key( 0, prompt => $doc{prompt} );
  if ( $doc{app} ) {
    $out .= "# subagents of subagents: raider allows that only above its default depth of 1\n";
    $out .= dump_key( 0, app => $doc{app} );
  }
  $out .= join '', map { '# '.$_."\n" } map { redact( plain_paths( $ctx, $_ ) ) } @{ $ctx->{file_notes} };
  $out .= dump_key( 0, files => $doc{files} ) if $doc{files};
  $out .= dump_key( 0, home => $doc{home} )   if $doc{home};
  $out .= "script:\n";
  for my $item (@items) {
    $out .= comments( 2, $item->{comments} ).dump_item( 2, flowed( $item->{step} ) );
  }
  $out .= comments( 2, \@pending );
  $out .= "expect:\n".dump_key( 2, answer => $doc{expect}{answer} );
  if (@tools) {
    $out .= "  tools:\n";
    $out .= comments( 4, $_->{comments} ).dump_item( 4, flow_or_block( $_->{want} ) ) for @tools;
  }

  my $back = YAML::PP->new( boolean => 'JSON::PP' )->load_string($out);
  my $where = first_difference( \%doc, $back, '' );
  croak 'The scenario does not read back as written at '.$where.' (a YAML writing problem)' if defined $where;
  return $out;
}

# Where two data structures part, or undef when they do not.
sub first_difference {
  my ( $want, $got, $where ) = @_;
  if ( ref $want eq 'HASH' && ref $got eq 'HASH' ) {
    for my $key ( sort keys %{ { %$want, %$got } } ) {
      my $d = first_difference( $want->{$key}, $got->{$key}, $where.'/'.$key );
      return $d if defined $d;
    }
    return;
  }
  if ( ref $want eq 'ARRAY' && ref $got eq 'ARRAY' ) {
    for my $i ( 0 .. ( $#$want > $#$got ? $#$want : $#$got ) ) {
      my $d = first_difference( $want->[$i], $got->[$i], $where.'/'.$i );
      return $d if defined $d;
    }
    return;
  }
  return $JSON->encode( [$want] ) eq $JSON->encode( [$got] ) ? undef : $where || '/';
}

sub default_title {
  my ( $ctx, $log, $prompts ) = @_;
  my ($prompt) = grep { defined } @$prompts;
  return one_line( $prompt, 72 ) if defined $prompt && $prompt =~ /\S/;
  return 'a section of Claude Code session '.$log->{file}->basename('.jsonl');
}

sub header {
  my ( $log, $section, $ctx ) = @_;
  my $start = $section->{start};
  my @lines = (
    'DRAFT -- written by maint/claude-log-to-scenario from Claude Code session',
    $log->{file}->basename('.jsonl').', from record '.( $start->{uuid} // '?' ).' ('.( $start->{time} // '?' ).'),',
    $section->{taken}.' model response'.( $section->{taken} == 1 ? '' : 's' )
      .( $ctx->{sub_steps} ? ' and '.$ctx->{sub_steps}.' of subagents' : '' ).'. Curate it before it goes into t/scenarios/:',
    '- files: holds what the session showed in full of each file before changing it;',
    '- tool calls raider has no counterpart for are left out (noted where they were);',
    ( $ctx->{depth} ? '- a subagent replays its own log right after the call that starts it;' : () ),
    '- the expect: anchors are guesses, raider words results and errors its own way;',
    '- secrets are REDACTED, the project path is {{ROOT}}, the home {{HOME}};',
    '- the bash commands run for real when the scenario runs: read them first.',
  );
  return join( '', map { '# '.$_."\n" } @lines )."\n";
}

sub comments {
  my ( $indent, $lines ) = @_;
  return join '', map { ( ' ' x $indent ).'# '.$_."\n" } map { split /\n/ } @{ $lines // [] };
}

sub dump_key {
  my ( $indent, $key, $value ) = @_;
  return indent( $indent, $YAML->dump_string( ordered( { $key => $value } ) ) );
}

sub dump_item {
  my ( $indent, $value ) = @_;
  return indent( $indent, $YAML->dump_string( ordered( [$value] ) ) );
}

sub indent {
  my ( $indent, $text ) = @_;
  $text =~ s/\A---\n//;
  # YAML::PP ends a document whose last scalar keeps its trailing newlines
  # (|+) with "...": inside a larger document that would end it early.
  $text =~ s/^\.\.\.\n\z//m;
  my $pad = ' ' x $indent;
  $text =~ s/^(?=.)/$pad/mg;
  return $text;
}

# A step with its tool calls in flow style ([ read_file, { path: a.txt } ])
# where that stays on one short line.
sub flowed {
  my ( $step ) = @_;
  return $step unless $step->{tool_calls};
  return { tool_calls => [ map { flow_or_block($_) } @{ $step->{tool_calls} } ] };
}

sub flow_or_block {
  my ( $value ) = @_;
  my $multi_line = 0;
  deep( sub { $multi_line ||= $_[0] =~ /[\n\r]/; $_[0] }, $value );
  return $value if $multi_line;
  my $flow = flow($value);
  my $line = $YAML->dump_string( [$flow] );
  return length($line) <= 110 ? $flow : $value;
}

# Mappings with their keys in a fixed order (YAML::PP keeps the order of
# preserved mappings only; plain ones would come out in hash order).
sub ordered {
  my ( $v ) = @_;
  return $v if ( ref $v eq 'HASH' && tied %$v ) || ( ref $v eq 'ARRAY' && tied @$v );
  if ( ref $v eq 'HASH' ) {
    my $m = $YAML->preserved_mapping( {} );
    $m->{$_} = ordered( $v->{$_} ) for sort_keys($v);
    return $m;
  }
  return [ map { ordered($_) } @$v ] if ref $v eq 'ARRAY';
  return $v;
}

sub sort_keys {
  my ( $hash ) = @_;
  return sort { ( $KEY_RANK{$a} // 9 ) <=> ( $KEY_RANK{$b} // 9 ) || $a cmp $b } keys %$hash;
}

sub flow {
  my ( $v ) = @_;
  if ( ref $v eq 'HASH' ) {
    my $m = $YAML->preserved_mapping( {}, style => YAML_FLOW_MAPPING_STYLE );
    $m->{$_} = flow( $v->{$_} ) for sort_keys($v);
    return $m;
  }
  return $YAML->preserved_sequence( [ map { flow($_) } @$v ], style => YAML_FLOW_SEQUENCE_STYLE ) if ref $v eq 'ARRAY';
  return $v;
}

# A clean message for the person at the terminal, not a stack of main:: frames.
my $exit = eval { main() };
unless ( defined $exit ) {
  ( my $error = $@ ) =~ s/ at \S+ line [0-9]+\.?\n.*\z//s;
  print STDERR 'claude-log-to-scenario: '.$error."\n";
  $exit = 2;
}
exit $exit;
